speechtext:
Madam Speaker, there have been discussions among the Parties and I believe that you would find that there is consent for two motions to be put and dealt with. The first motion is as follows:
That the Standing Committee on Finance and Economic Affairs be
empowered to travel to Vancouver, Edmonton, Regina and Winnipeg from
September 20 to September 25, 1987;
to Quebec City, Fredericton, Charlottetown, Halifax and St. John's
(Newfoundland) from September 27 to September 30, 1987;
to Mont Ste-Marie (Quebec) on October 13, 14 and 15, 1987, for the
purpose of drafting its report to the House;
and that the necessary staff do accompany the committee.
